<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ronda</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ronda is a town in the mountains of Málaga province in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andalusia">Andalusia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, built on either side of a deep gorge cut by the Guadalevín river. Under Muslim rule it was the centre of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> kingdom in the 11th century and later a frontier fortress of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>. The Catholic Monarchs captured it in 1485, and its 18th-century Puente Nuevo bridge and bullring are famous.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ronda.jpg" alt="Ronda" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: kallerna · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ronda_aerial.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
